    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§2 & 13, Chap 405 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7133\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 405 of the laws of 2011, relating to\nauthorizing the lease of lands located at the state university of New\nYork at Purchase, in relation to extending the authorization for the\nlength of leased land; and in relation to removing prior approval for\ncontracts or leases by the attorney general, director of budget and\nstate comptroller\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would amend Chapter 405 of the Laws of 2011 for the\ndevelopment of a senior learning community (SLC).\n\nSection 1. Section 2 of Chapter 405 of the Laws of 2011 is amended by\nchanging the lease term from \"forty\" to \"seventy-five\" years.\n\nSection 2. Section 13 of Chapter 405 of the Laws of 2011 is amended to\nbring the Chapter into conformance with the current procurement\npractices of the State University of New York.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe purpose of the Senior Learning Community (SLC) is to integrate\nseniors with an interest in the arts and education with students and\nfaculty to enhance the overall learning experience for all involved,\nspecifically the students. Any and all proceeds from this lease are\ndirected to fund student financial aid for students who are eligible\nfor tuition assistance program (TAP) or supplemental tuition\nassistance, as well as funding for full-time faculty. By making the\nchanges above, the project will attract better financing options and\nhave lower administrative costs.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately\n",
